msgid "ROS CLI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Scripts.rst:18
msgid ""
"In ROS 1 there were individual commands for performing various actions, like "
"``rosrun``, ``rosparam``, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Scripts.rst:20
msgid ""
"In ROS 2, there is a single top-level commands called ``ros2``, and all of "
"the actions are sub-commands of that, like ``ros2 run``, ``ros2 param``, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Scripts.rst:23
msgid "ROS CLI arguments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Scripts.rst:25
msgid ""
"In ROS 1, arguments to nodes were provided directly on the command-line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Scripts.rst:27
msgid ""
"ROS 2 arguments should be scoped with ``--ros-args`` and a trailing ``--`` "
"(the trailing double dash may be elided if no arguments follow it)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Scripts.rst:29
msgid ""
"Remapping names is similar to ROS 1, taking on the form ``from:=to``, except "
"that it must be preceded by a ``--remap`` (or ``-r``) flag. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Scripts.rst:32
msgid "$ ros2 run some_package some_ros_executable --ros-args -r foo:=bar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Scripts.rst:36
msgid ""
"We use a similar syntax for parameters, using the ``--param`` (or ``-p``) "
"flag:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Scripts.rst:38
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run some_package some_ros_executable --ros-args -p my_param:=value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Scripts.rst:42
msgid "Note, this is different than using a leading underscore in ROS 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Scripts.rst:44
msgid ""
"To change a node name use ``__node`` (the ROS 1 equivalent is ``__name``):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Scripts.rst:46
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run some_package some_ros_executable --ros-args -r __node:"
"=new_node_name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Scripts.rst:50
msgid ""
"Note the use of the ``-r`` flag. The same remap flag is needed for changing "
"the namespace ``__ns``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Scripts.rst:53
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run some_package some_ros_executable --ros-args -r __ns:=/new/"
"namespace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Scripts.rst:57
msgid "There is no equivalent in ROS 2 for the following ROS 1 keys:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Scripts.rst:59
msgid ""
"``__log`` (but ``--log-config-file`` can be used to provide a logger "
"configuration file)"
